<title>USA: World Centrifugal Sugar Production -- USDA.</title>
<headline>World Centrifugal Sugar Production -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Wednesday released following table in its World Agricultural Production report:</p>
<p>		     WORLD CENTRIFUGAL SUGAR PRODUCTION</p>
<p>				(1,000 Metric tons)</p>
<p>			     1994/95     1995/96	 As of	 As of</p>
<p>								 11/96	  3/97</p>
<p>Western Hemisphere</p>
<p>	 Argentina	   1,180	 1,590	 1,320	 1,380</p>
<p>	 Brazil	     12,500	13,700	14,500	14,650</p>
<p>	 Colombia	    2,071	 2,002	 2,030	 2,030</p>
<p>	 Cuba		  3,300	 4,450	 4,600	 4,600</p>
<p>	 Guatemala	   1,333	 1,334	 1,440	 1,440</p>
<p>	 Mexico		4,556	 4,660	 4,600	 4,700</p>
<p>	 United State	7,191	 6,686	 6,468	 6,563</p>
<p>    European Union	16,533	17,005	17,244	17,724</p>
<p>	 France		4,363	 4,601	 4,400	 4,560</p>
<p>	 Germany	     3,991	 4,150	 4,550	 4,550</p>
<p>	 Italy		 1,622	 1,621	 1,460	 1,560</p>
<p>	 Netherlands	 1,050	 1,085	 1,100	 1,120</p>
<p>	 Spain		 1,214	 1,195	 1,200	 1,250</p>
<p>	 United Kingd	1,373	 1,330	 1,500	 1,500</p>
<p>Eastern Europe</p>
<p>	  Poland	     1,492	 1,714	 2,200	 2,446</p>
<p>FSU</p>
<p>	  Russia	     1,655	 2,060	 1,900	 1,750</p>
<p>	  Ukraine	    3,600	 3,800	 3,000	 2,900</p>
<p>Africa</p>
<p>	 Egypt		 1,088	 1,109	 1,250	 1,250</p>
<p>	 South Africa	1,770	 1,769	 2,500	 2,400</p>
<p>Middle East</p>
<p>	 Turkey		1,678	 1,375	 2,000	 2,000</p>
<p>Asia</p>
<p>	 China		 5,900	 6,750	 7,000	 7,000</p>
<p>	 India 3/	   16,410	18,270	17,000	15,600</p>
<p>	 Indonesia	   2,450	 2,100	 2,450	 2,450</p>
<p>	 Pakistan	    3,212	 2,643	 2,800	 2,600</p>
<p>	 Philippines	 1,647	 1,787	 1,850	 1,800</p>
<p>	 Thailand	    5,448	 6,300	 6,500	 6,300</p>
<p>Oceania</p>
<p>	 Australia	   5,196	 5,136	 5,600	 5,600</p>
<p>    Others		  15,552	16,214	16,737	16,771</p>
<p>    WORLD		  115,762     122,454     124,989     123,954</p>
<p>1/ Includes Puerto Rico.</p>
<p>2/ Total EU sugar production excludes French</p>
<p>overseas departments.</p>
<p>3/ The EC now includes Austria, Finland, and Sweden which</p>
<p>became members January 1, 1995.</p>
<p>4/ Includes khandsari sugar in thousands of tons</p>
<p>(raw value equivalent)as follows: 1994/95 - 720; 1995/96 - 620; 1996/97 - 620.</p>
</text>
